    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27286" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διόρ-υγμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cut, canal,</i> as that across the isthmus of Mount Athos,
				<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.109
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>digging through, house-breaking,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				22.2(1)
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Je.</u>
				2.34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>hole made in wall by</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χελώνη,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				32.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>siege-mine,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				20.94
			</span></i>.</div>
